/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:128:Recolor a cropped template and repeat it according to a component-count stencil.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:129:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:130:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:131:- Solid blue (1) separator rows or columns split the grid into four sections.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:132:- Section 1 is a black-background shape template; section 2 is a component-count stencil.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:133:- Sections 3 and 4 are solid color swatches for output foreground and background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:134:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:135:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:136:- Crop section 1 to the bbox of its non-black pixels and recolor it with the two swatches.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:137:- Count 4-connected non-black components in section 2.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:138:- Repeat the recolored crop that many times, inserting one background-colored row/column between copies.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:139:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:140:Key insight: The second section encodes only the repeat count; the output orientation
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:141:is inherited from whether the input separators are columns or rows.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:142:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:143:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:144:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:145:<reference_puzzle index="8" source="train" puzzle_id="b7955b3c" lines="386-403">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:146:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:147:Replace gray plus-shaped damage masks with the hidden colors of the rectilinear mosaic.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:148:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:149:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:150:- Color 8 appears only as isolated 3x3 plus masks.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:151:- The non-mask pixels are visible parts of a clean grid made from horizontal
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:152:  and vertical color regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:153:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:154:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:155:- Treat every color-8 pixel as unknown damage and leave all other pixels fixed.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:156:- First copy unknown pixels from exact matching parallel rows or columns.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:157:- Then fill any remaining mask cells from opposite-side continuations and the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:158:  better-supported local straight edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:159:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:160:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:161:- The gray pluses are occluders, not objects; the underlying colors are
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:162:  determined by repeated line templates and nearby axis-aligned boundaries.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:163:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:164:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:165:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:166:<reference_puzzle index="9" source="eval" puzzle_id="de809cff" lines="86-103">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:167:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:168:Turn black dents in two colored regions into marked opposite-color patches.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:169:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:170:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:171:- Black background with two large foreground colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:172:- The large regions contain small black dents and a few one-cell color specks
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:173:  or protrusions along region boundaries.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:174:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:175:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:176:- Locally clean the two foreground regions: isolated specks become black, and
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:177:  one-cell protrusions surrounded by the other region take that region's color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:178:- Each original black dent whose cleaned 3x3 neighborhood is mostly one
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:179:  foreground color becomes the center of a 3x3 patch in the opposite color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:180:- The dent center itself is recolored teal (8).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:181:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:182:Key insight: The teal pixels mark the original black defects; the surrounding
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:183:3x3 patch uses the other foreground color, after first removing boundary noise.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:184:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:185:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:186:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:187:<reference_puzzle index="10" source="eval" puzzle_id="136b0064" lines="25-39">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:188:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:189:Draw a polyline by decoding 3x3 glyph instructions read across a divided grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:190:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:191:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:192:- Left of a full-height vertical divider: 3x3 colored glyphs on bg.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:193:- Right of divider: a single gray (5) start pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:194:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:195:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:196:- Remove the divider; shift the gray start into the left canvas.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:197:- Read glyphs in column-major order (left→right, top→bottom).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:198:- Each glyph's shape (pixel area) encodes a segment: area 4 → down 2, area 5 → right 3, area 6 → left 4, area 7 → left 2.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:199:- Append segments sequentially, stepping down one cell between each.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:200:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:201:Key insight: Glyph pixel count (area) uniquely determines both segment length and direction — the shape itself is the instruction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:202:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:203:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:204:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:205:<reference_puzzle index="11" source="train" puzzle_id="ac6f9922" lines="18-40">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:206:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:207:Summarize the enclosed table slots by the single object color inside each slot, using the slot background color for empty slots.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:208:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:209:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:210:- The most common color forms the outer background and all enclosed slot
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:211:  backgrounds.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:212:- The enclosed background components form a complete rectangular array of
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:213:  slots, ordered by their positions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:214:- Each slot contains either no other color or exactly one object color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:215:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:216:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:217:- Find all 4-connected components of the most common color that do not touch
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:218:  the input edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:219:- Sort their bounding boxes into row and column order to define the output
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:220:  table.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:221:- For each slot, output its unique non-background color if present; otherwise
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:222:  output the background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:223:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:224:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:225:- The large grid is an expanded table: the enclosed background components are
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:226:  the cells, and any colored object drawn inside a cell is that cell's summary
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:227:  value.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:228:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:229:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:230:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:231:<reference_puzzle index="12" source="train" puzzle_id="df9fd884" lines="33-47">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:232:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:233:Move the colored object from the lower bracket lane to the upper bracket lane and drop it to the bottom edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:234:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:235:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:236:- The background is the dominant color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:237:- One frame color forms exactly two 4-connected bracket objects: a top-edge bracket open downward and a bottom-edge bracket open upward.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:238:- One other 4-connected foreground object sits in the lower bracket's interior column span.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:239:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:240:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:241:- Remove the movable object from its original cells.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:242:- Keep its shape and color unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:243:- Paste it with its bbox columns aligned to the top bracket's interior columns and with its bbox bottom aligned to the grid bottom.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:244:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:245:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:246:- The lower bracket identifies the object's source lane; the upper bracket provides the target lane, and the final vertical placement is bottom-aligned.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:247:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:248:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:249:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:250:<reference_puzzle index="13" source="train" puzzle_id="d6542281" lines="72-91">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:251:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:252:Complete each partial marker mask by stamping the matching multicolor sprite over it.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:253:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:254:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:255:- A dominant background contains one or more 8-connected multicolor sprites.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:256:- Separate target masks use colors that already occur inside one of those sprites.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:257:- A target mask may contain only one marker pixel or several same-alignment marker pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:258:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:259:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:260:- For each multicolor sprite, test every translation that aligns a target pixel with a
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:261:  same-color sprite pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:262:- Keep the translations with maximal exact overlap against the existing target pixels,
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:263:  rejecting translations that conflict with other foreground or overlap a source sprite.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:264:- Stamp the whole sprite at those translations; if a non-marker sprite color occurs as
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:265:  a single source pixel, consume that source-only marker back to background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:266:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:267:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:268:The scattered target pixels are partial copies: their same-color overlap with a sprite
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:269:determines where the full sprite must be completed.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:270:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:271:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:272:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:273:<reference_puzzle index="14" source="train" puzzle_id="c9680e90" lines="52-67">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:274:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:275:Move each mirrored bottom source pixel to the far end of its trail and redraw the top half as its reflection.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:276:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:277:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:278:- A solid non-background row separates equal-height top and bottom halves.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:279:- The top half has one marker color on the background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:280:- In the bottom half, exactly one color has positions that mirror the top markers across the separator, and the other color forms trails touching those source pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:281:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:282:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:283:- Identify the bottom source color by reflecting each bottom color into the top half and matching the top marker set.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:284:- For every bottom source pixel, follow its unique 4-connected trail of the other bottom color to the trail endpoint.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:285:- Clear the old top markers, bottom sources, and trails; place the source color at each endpoint and place the top marker color at the reflected endpoint.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:286:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:287:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:288:- The top half is only a mirror display of the bottom moving sources; the actual motion is encoded by the trail attached to each bottom source pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:289:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:290:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:291:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:292:<reference_puzzle index="15" source="train" puzzle_id="902510d5" lines="58-80">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:293:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:294:Keep the largest 8-connected motif and replace the corner/control pixels with a solid corner triangle.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:295:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:296:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:297:- The background is the dominant color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:298:- Exactly one grid corner contains a foreground control pixel; it gives the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:299:  corner from which the triangle is painted.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:300:- There is one unique largest 8-connected monochrome foreground object, the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:301:  motif that remains in the output; all other foreground pixels are controls.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:302:- Every foreground component outside that motif is a singleton control pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:303:- The fill color is the unique control color that appears in at least two
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:304:  non-corner control pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:305:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:306:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:307:- Start from a blank background canvas and redraw only the largest motif.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:308:- Count the non-corner control pixels; that count is the triangle side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:309:- Paint the fill color on the right-triangle region where those two distances
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:310:  from the marked corner's edges sum to less than the side length.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:311:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:312:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:313:- The scattered singleton controls are counted into a compact triangular
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:314:  stack at the marked corner; only the largest motif is not part of the count.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:315:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:316:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:317:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:318:<reference_puzzle index="16" source="train" puzzle_id="252143c9" lines="14-33">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:319:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:320:Keep only the center color and redraw it as a diagonal ray to its indicated corner.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:321:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:322:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:323:- The grid is an odd square with a unique dominant background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:324:- The center pixel is foreground.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:325:- Every off-center pixel with the center color lies in the same diagonal
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:326:  quadrant relative to the center.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:327:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:328:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:329:- Fill the whole output with the background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:330:- Use the quadrant of the center-colored pixels to choose one diagonal
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/16/prompt.md:331:  direction from the center.
